              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for the spine, then the Telugu for breath."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: చూపు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చూపు — cūpu — \"eyesight; a look\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వయసుతో తాతయ్య చూపు తగ్గింది. vayasutō tātayya cūpu taggindi. With age grandpa's eyesight has weakened."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Also a glance: ఒక చూపు (cūpu), one look. The noun of చూడు, to see."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చూపు (cūpu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 2735 lists Telugu cūcu, \"to see\", and cūpu, \"sight, vision, look, glance\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
